  "lineage": "Turkish-language tango song that flourished in Istanbul from the 1930s into the 1950s, after Argentine and European tango reached the city's dance halls and gramophone market. Necip Celal Andel is credited with composing the first Turkish tangos, singers such as Seyyan Hanım and İbrahim Özgür recorded the repertoire on 78rpm discs, and the songs set Turkish lyrics of longing to the four-beat tango rhythm, accompanied by small Western-style dance orchestras of violin, piano and bass.",
